bird, leaf, and blossoms like a continent of butterfliesW:breathing on the wind. And peering through, color sky from iron to blue.W:W:Hold summer in your hand, pour summer in a glass, a tiny glass of course,W:the smallest tingling sip for children; change the season in your veins by raisingW:glass to lip and tilting summer in."W:W:-- Ray Bradbury, Dandelion WineX:6T:Jour d'eteT:Summer DayO:FranceC:F. ParisR:SchottischeM:4/4L:1/8K:G%% text Scottisch|:"G"BdcA B2G2|BdcA "C"G4|EFG2 GAB2|"D"cBAc "G"B2G2|\"G"BdcA B2G2|BdcA "C"G4|EFG2 GABG|"D"cAFA "G"G4:||:"C"efef e3f|efef "G"d4|"C"edc2 cBAB|"D"cBAc "G"B2G2|\"C"efef e3f|efef "G"d4|"C"edc2 cBAB|"D"cAFA "G"G4:|X:7T: Autumn in AmherstT:The Red Star LineC:Kathy TalvitieZ:ssgM:2/2L:1/8K:DAG|"D"F3G "A7"E2FG|"Bm"F2ED "G"B,DA,D|"D/f#"A,2AG"Bm"F2D2|"Em"G3F "A7"EFGB|"D"A3G"Bm"F2(3FGA|"G"d3c "A7"BAFE|"Bm"D2dc "G"B2"D"A2|"Em"G2"D"F2"A7"E2EF||"G"D3B"A7"A2FE|"Bm"DEFd"G"B2(3dcB|"D"A3G"Bm"F2ED|"Em"G3"D"F "A7"EDCA,|"Gmaj7"B,2DF "A7"EFGB|"D"A2cd"G"B2"A"c2|"Bm"d2"D/f#"A2"Em"GFED|"A7"E2DC"D"D4|]X:8T:Warm and SnugM:CL:1/8K:AAB|"A"cBcBA2EA|"D"FEFA "E"B2AB|"A"cBAe "D"fecA|"E"B4B2AB|"A"cBcBA2EA|"D"FEFA "E"B2AB|"A"cBAe "D"fecA|"E"B4"A"A2:|AB|"A"c2cde2ce|"D"fefg a2AB|"A"cBce "D"fecA|"E"B4B2AB|"A"c2cde2ce|"D"fefg a2AB|"A"cBce "D"fecA|"E"B4"A"A2AB|"A"c2cde2ce|"D"fefg a2AB|"A"cBce "D"fecA|"E"B4B2AB|"A"cBcBA2EA|"D"FEFA "E"B2AB|"A"cBAe "D"fecA|"E"B4"A"A2|]X:9T:Hot as PepperC:Rick Gagne (RIP 2014)F:rickfile/2045hap%---F: http://www.capeirish.com/webabc/working/source.folders/rick/rick_plus/2045hap.pdf%%gchordfont Times-Roman 16Z: abc-edited-by: Adlai Waksman (Oct. 2020) for SPUDS (open band of the Mt. Airy Contra Dance, Philadelphia)%---N:1989 on tenor banjoQ:180M:4/4K:Ador|:^ce|"A"a2a^g- g aae|"G"gedB cAG2|"F"AB c/B/A "Em"B2ga|"G"gede "Em"g2e2| "A"a2a^g- g aae|"G"gedB cAG2|"F"AB c/B/A "Em"B2ga|"G"gedB .|[1"Am"A2:|[2"Am"A4|||:"F"AB c/B/A "Em"B2ga|"G"gede "Em"gedB|"F"AB c/B/A "Em"B2ga|"G"ged